{"event": "llm_start", "tag": "write", "prompt": "A research paper introduces this recurrent sequence layer. Its reference implementation is a Python loop\nover time:\n\n```python\ndef reference(q, k, v, e, g, beta, gamma, scale):\n    # q, k, e: [B, H, T, K] (k, e unit-norm); v: [B, H, T, V]; g (log decay, <= 0): [B, H, T, K];\n    # beta, gamma in (0, 1): [B, H, T]\n    B, H, T, K = q.shape\n    V = v.shape[-1]\n    q, k, v, e, g, beta, gamma = (x.to(torch.promote_types(x.dtype, torch.float32))\n                                  for x in (q, k, v, e, g, beta, gamma))\n    S = q.new_zeros(B, H, K, V)\n    outs = []\n    for t in range(T):\n        kt, vt, et, bt = k[:, :, t], v[:, :, t], e[:, :, t], beta[:, :, t]\n        ct = gamma[:, :, t]\n        S = S * g[:, :, t].exp()[..., None]\n        pred = (S * kt[..., None]).sum(-2)\n        S = S + (bt[..., None] * (vt - pred))[..., None, :] * kt[..., None]\n        S = S + ct[..., None, None] * et[..., None] * vt[..., None, :]\n        outs.append((S * (q[:, :, t] * scale)[..., None]).sum(-2))\n    return torch.stack(outs, dim=2)\n```\n\nIn matrix form, with state S of shape [K, V]: S_t = (I - beta_t k_t k_t^T) diag(exp g_t) S_{t-1} + beta_t k_t v_t^T + gamma_t e_t v_t^T (a second, additive write along e),    o_t = scale * S_t^T q_t unless stated otherwise. Inputs the equation does not use are still passed.\n\nThe loop takes 192 ms forward at B=4, H=8, T=2048, K=V=128 on an NVIDIA L4, too slow to train\nwith. Write a fast Triton implementation for the L4 (Ada, sm_89, Triton 3.5).\n\nRequirements:\n- Define `def kernel_function(q, k, v, e, g, beta, gamma, scale):` with the reference's argument order, shapes and semantics,\n  returning a [B, H, T, V] tensor (float32 or q's dtype). q, k, v, e arrive as bf16, g, beta and gamma as fp32.\n- It must match the reference on any inputs the reference accepts.\n- The computation must happen in your own @triton.jit kernels; the Python wrapper may only allocate, reshape,\n  launch and do cheap elementwise prep. Do not import or copy any existing implementation of this layer.\n\nYou cannot run anything. Return the complete module in one ```python block, then 2-4 sentences on your\napproach and anything you are unsure about.", "t": 1793086268.545902}
